@page "/privacy/receipt-importer"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Receipt importer privacy policy - Group Split</PageTitle>

<article class="gs-receipt-privacy">
    <a href="/">Group Split</a>
    <h1>Receipt importer privacy policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: November 3, 2026</p>
    <p>The GroupSplit receipt importer helps you import selected purchases from Amazon and Costco into your GroupSplit receipts inbox using Microsoft Edge. You choose when to connect a store and start an import.</p>

    <h2>Information the importer uses</h2>
    <p>For Amazon, the importer reads order dates, items, quantities, prices, shipping, tax and totals. It reads ship-to recipient names for the optional recipient filter and uses the order identifier to create a reference for duplicate detection. Recipient names are used locally for filtering and are not included in the generated receipt or sent to GroupSplit.</p>
    <p>The Amazon receipt is a newly generated summary. It does not copy the original invoice's customer, address or payment sections. Item names can themselves contain personal information, so review them before importing.</p>
    <p>For Costco warehouse purchases, the importer reads receipt listings and prints the displayed receipt to PDF. A Costco receipt may include customer or membership information and masked payment details. Costco online orders are not supported by this preview.</p>
    <p>You sign in directly to the retailer. The extension uses your existing browser session and does not ask for or store your retailer password.</p>

    <h2>Where information goes</h2>
    <p>When you choose to import receipts, the extension creates a PDF in your browser and uploads it to your signed-in GroupSplit inbox without downloading a copy to your device. For new Amazon receipts, it also sends the extracted items and totals to GroupSplit. GroupSplit stores uploaded receipts under your account.</p>
    <p>The extension does not configure analytics or send retailer data to an additional third-party service. Retailers and Microsoft Edge handle their own requests under their respective policies.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>You decide which retailer to connect and when to start an import. You can review results before importing, and remove receipts from GroupSplit. You can also remove the extension or revoke its site permissions in Microsoft Edge.</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions or requests about your GroupSplit data, sign in and use the <a href="/help">GroupSplit help page</a>. Please do not include passwords or payment details in a support request.</p>
</article>

